# The maintenance job's timer (SPEC-027, SPEC-032; ADR-027): once a day, at the rollover hour,
# minute 28. The job table in crates/coordination/src/jobs.rs is the one schedule, and
# crates/coordination/tests/job_table.rs holds this calendar equal to it. The calendar is written in
# UTC, the neutral zone, at the default rollover hour; the private rail renders the deployment's own
# zone and hour (deploy/README.md). With no Unit=, the timer starts the job instance of its own name.
# Run this job by hand only at its slot: a run off its slot makes the next liveness check page a
# drift, once (ADR-027).
[Unit]
Description=DeckStreak's daily maintenance, at the rollover hour, minute 28
X-DurableServices-Waive=calendar-not-persistent the job table makes maintenance no catch-up job (ADR-027): a run missed while the host was down waits for its next slot, where the drift check expects it
X-DurableServices-Waive=randomized-delay-missing the job table places each job on its own minute (ADR-027), and a random delay would move each fire off its minute

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 04:28:00 UTC

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
